course: dictionary
lesson: 1545
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it: this is the context. «Chalky» can mean made of chalk, pale like chalk, or dry and powdery.
explain: In a geography lesson, «chalky cliffs» tells you about the land: the rock is soft and white, like the White Cliffs of Dover. In a story, «a chalky face» is about a person, and it means very pale, often from fear or illness. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «chalky» meant made of chalk, then «a chalky face» would make no sense for a person, so pale is the right meaning there.
fact: Chalky is an adjective: chalky, chalkier, chalkiest.
fact: «Chalky soil» or «chalky cliffs» means containing chalk or made of chalk.
fact: Chalk is a soft white rock that formed from tiny sea creatures.
fact: «A chalky face» means white and pale, like chalk.
fact: «Chalky tablets» means dry and powdery.
exercise: «The White Cliffs of Dover are chalky.» What does chalky mean here? | Covered in mud | Pale and frightened | Dry and powdery | *Made of chalk
exercise: Lily's face went chalky when she heard the news. What does chalky mean here? | Dry and powdery | *Very pale, like chalk | Made of chalk | Shiny and wet
exercise: «The tablets were chalky and crumbled in my fingers.» What does chalky mean here? | Very pale with fear | Made of soft white rock | Sticky and wet | *Dry and powdery
test: «The chalky hills of the South Downs were rounded and white.» Which meaning fits best? | *Containing or made of chalk | Pale like a ghost | Sticky and wet | Dry and powdery
test: After the playground, Sam's hands were chalky from the drawings. Which meaning fits best? | Very pale with fear | *Dry and powdery, with white dust | Made of soft white rock | Cold and wet
exam: Which meaning of chalky means very pale, often from fear or illness? | Smooth and shiny | *White and pale like chalk | Dry and powdery | Containing chalk
